  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "Using the Synthetic Control Method on monthly registration data from January 2018 to March 2025, this study analyzed the causal impact of Germany's sudden, court-mandated termination of battery electric vehicle (BEV) subsidies in December 2023. The abrupt policy end resulted in an estimated 45% decline in the German BEV market, translating to approximately 140,000 forgone registrations in 2024.",
      "why": "It provides the first empirical, real-world measurement of how an unexpected and immediate withdrawal of financial incentives affects electric vehicle adoption, demonstrating that market stability and decarbonization trajectories are highly vulnerable to sudden policy shifts."
    }
